            "text": "<p><strong>Champagne Lasseaux: A Legacy of Passion and Excellence</strong></p><p><strong>Roots in Tradition:</strong> In the heart of the Marne Valley, Neuville-aux-Larris is where the story of Champagne Lasseaux begins. Claire Simone Geoffroy, grandmother of Baptiste and Vincent, laid the foundation. Born in 1922, she united with Jean-Louis Lasseaux in 1949, growing the family.</p><p><strong>Growing Through Generations:</strong> Jean-Louis' son, Philippe, learned alongside his father and embraced vineyard work. Expanding the vineyards, he planted Pinot Noir and Meunier, forming Champagne Lasseaux. The brand evolved, becoming Champagne Lasseaux and Fils in 2010.</p><p><strong>Generation change:</strong> Philippe handed down his 2.5-hectare legacy to his sons, Vincent and Baptiste. Vincent is focused on export and digital presence, while Baptiste is managing vineyard and cellar work, nurturing the brand.</p><p><strong>Tradition and Innovation:</strong> The Lasseaux brothers carry on their family's resilient spirit. With 6.5 hectares, they blend tradition with modernity, emphasizing terroir and expertise in crafting exceptional French champagne.\"</p><p><em>Champagne Lasseaux, Tradition, Terroir, Excellence, Family Legacy, Vineyards, Marne Valley, Passion, Craftsmanship.</em></p><p><a href=\"https://champagne-season.com/blogs/all-blogs/about-lasseaux\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://champagne-season.com/blogs/all-blogs/about-lasseaux\"><strong>Click here to learn more about Lasseaux</strong></a></p>",
